### Cause
In [app/build.gradle.kts](file:///C:/Users/vinuj/Downloads/Pixel-Funds-main/app/build.gradle.kts#L33-L38), the `debug` build type was hardcoded to use a custom `debugConfig` signing configuration pointing to `${rootDir}/debug.keystore`. Because `debug.keystore` is excluded by [.gitignore](file:///C:/Users/vinuj/Downloads/Pixel-Funds-main/.gitignore#L18), that file does not exist in a fresh download/clone, causing `:app:validateSigningDebug` to fail.

### How I Fixed It
Updated the `debug` build type in [app/build.gradle.kts](file:///C:/Users/vinuj/Downloads/Pixel-Funds-main/app/build.gradle.kts#L50-L59) to check whether `${rootDir}/debug.keystore` exists:
- If it **does** exist (for example, in AI Studio), it still uses `signingConfigs.getByName("debugConfig")`.
- If it **does not** exist locally, it falls back to Android Gradle Plugin's built-in `signingConfigs.getByName("debug")` (which uses `~/.android/debug.keystore` and auto-generates it if missing).

